# Feed recorded flight data into the emulated sensors.
#
# Run after startup.resc, once the board has finished MRT_Init. The LSM6DSR feeds
# need the output data rate, which resets to Disabled and is only set by the driver
# during init - feeding earlier fails with "Frequency must be higher than zero".
#
# The models use StartExactSampleFeedThread, which takes no sampling rate: playback
# is paced by the timestamps in the RESD block, and feed() passes
# RESDStreamSampleOffset.CurrentVirtualTime so the log is rebased onto the machine's
# current virtual time. Without that, every sample is in the past and Renode
# discards the whole file ("RESD: Skipping sample").
#
# There is no quiet_first option: Renode 1.17 exposes no global log-level setter from
# Monitor Python, so the register-warning flood cannot be silenced. Completion is
# reported to %TEMP%\renode_resd_status.txt instead - check it with:
#
#     python "feedstatus()"
#
# Playback takes ~3.5 minutes of wall clock: the log is 61 s of emulated time and
# this board runs Renode at roughly 30% of real time.
#
# Change the argument to use a different file, or set $env:MRT_DATA_DIR and pass a
# bare filename.

python "feedall('data/data.resd')"